{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-01-14 09:59:04 UTC] [Agent: ArchitectAgent] [Project: council_web_ui] ARCHITECTURE COMPLETE - Council Web UI rebuild architecture fully designed and documented. Hybrid approach: keep production-ready backend (FastAPI+MCP+WebSocket), rebuild frontend (Web Components+SPA), add OAuth2+JWT auth. Architecture Guide: 3 sections (Problem Statement, Requirements with 28 FRs + 7 NFRs, Architecture Overview with system diagram + 4 components + data flows). Phase Plan: 5 phases, 19 task packages, 22-29 days estimated. All 36 Operations Guide boundary statements mapped to requirements. Ready for Coder Agent implementation. | confidence=0.95; documents_created=[\"ARCHITECTURE_GUIDE.md\", \"PHASE_PLAN.md\"]; operations_guide_compliance=all_36_boundary_statements_addressed; ready_for_implementation=True; reasoning={\"how\": \"Synthesized research reports (RESEARCH_EXISTING_WEBUI.md 559 lines, DESIGN_SYSTEM_GUIDE.md 797 lines, OPERATIONS_GUIDE.md 1161 lines with 36 boundary statements), verified backend code (app.py routes, auth integration points), designed auth system (OAuth2+JWT+user-persona mapping), designed frontend architecture (Web Components+Shadow DOM+SPA router), mapped Operations Guide compliance requirements (health system, command authority, cognitive load limits), broke into executable task packages\", \"what\": \"Created comprehensive ARCHITECTURE_GUIDE.md (system diagram, 4 components with module structures, authentication/API/WebSocket/health data flows, failure modes, integration points) and PHASE_PLAN.md (5 phases, 19 task packages, each with scope/files/specs/verification/dependencies). All requirements traced to research findings and Operations Guide boundary statements.\", \"why\": \"Complete architecture phase by delivering implementable design that Coder Agent can execute without ambiguity\"}; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/council_web_ui/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-14T09:59:04.549212+00:00_56169a0c", "timestamp": "2026-01-14T09:59:04.549245+00:00"}
