{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-01-14 10:08:13 UTC] [Agent: ReviewAgent] [Project: council_web_ui] FEASIBILITY ANALYSIS: Architecture is BUILDABLE with existing backend. Auth system design is standard (OAuth2+JWT+bcrypt), FastAPI has built-in support. Web Components are native browser API (no build step = feasible). Backend modifications minimal (add Depends(get_current_user) to routes). Phase 0 blocking strategy correct - auth must precede frontend work. Task package scoping excellent (1-3 files each, clear boundaries). Critical path identified correctly. Estimated 22-29 days is reasonable for scope. NO BLOCKERS FOUND. | confidence=0.95; evaluation_type=feasibility; reasoning={\"how\": \"Cross-referenced architecture against existing backend code structure, verified Web Components are browser-native, confirmed FastAPI auth patterns are standard, validated task package scoping\", \"what\": \"Evaluated technical feasibility: auth system (standard patterns), frontend architecture (native Web Components), backend integration (minimal changes), task scoping (appropriate), timeline (reasonable)\", \"why\": \"Feasibility determines if Coder Agent can execute without hitting impossible requirements\"}; verdict=buildable; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/council_web_ui/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-14T10:08:13.979617+00:00_c9b77d42", "timestamp": "2026-01-14T10:08:13.979645+00:00"}
{"op": "commit", "ref_id": "2026-01-14T10:08:13.979617+00:00_c9b77d42", "timestamp": "2026-01-14T10:08:13.989715+00:00"}
{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-01-14 10:08:14 UTC] [Agent: ReviewAgent] [Project: council_web_ui] SECURITY REVIEW: JWT implementation plan is SOLID. HS256 algorithm appropriate for single-instance deployment. Access token 15min expiry (good). Refresh token 7-day expiry stored as hash in DB (excellent - allows revocation). Password hashing with bcrypt/argon2 at cost 12+ (strong). Token validation in WebSocket handshake (correct pattern). All routes protected except /api/auth/* and /health (appropriate). Minor concern: Task 0.4 WebSocket auth uses query param for token (acceptable but header would be better - query params logged). Schema includes is_active flag (good for account disabling). Overall: NO CRITICAL SECURITY FLAWS. | concerns=[\"websocket_token_query_param\"]; confidence=0.93; evaluation_type=security; reasoning={\"how\": \"Reviewed auth specifications in Phase Plan Task 0.2-0.4, checked against OWASP best practices, verified token revocation capability, confirmed password hashing strength\", \"what\": \"Evaluated auth security: JWT signing (HS256 appropriate), token expiry (access 15min, refresh 7d), password hashing (bcrypt cost 12+), token storage (refresh hash in DB), WebSocket auth (token validation), route protection (comprehensive)\", \"why\": \"Security flaws discovered in architecture become vulnerabilities in production\"}; verdict=solid; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/council_web_ui/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-14T10:08:14.105185+00:00_91af6227", "timestamp": "2026-01-14T10:08:14.105216+00:00"}
{"op": "commit", "ref_id": "2026-01-14T10:08:14.105185+00:00_91af6227", "timestamp": "2026-01-14T10:08:14.117207+00:00"}
{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-01-14 10:08:14 UTC] [Agent: ReviewAgent] [Project: council_web_ui] OPERATIONS GUIDE COMPLIANCE VERIFICATION: All 36 boundary statements mapped to requirements/design. Health system (\u00a72): 4 states (HEALTHY/DEGRADED/FAILED/UNKNOWN) \u2705, 3 dimensions (Connection/Council/Scribe) \u2705, thresholds defined (FR-OPS-1 to FR-OPS-3) \u2705. Cognitive load (\u00a73): Decision vectors (3/7/1) \u2705, freeze-on-intent \u2705, temporal anchoring \u2705. Command authority (\u00a75): Read/Write/Mutate/Destroy classification \u2705, health-gated mutations \u2705, progressive disclosure for Destroy \u2705. Failure response (\u00a77): 6 failure modes documented \u2705. Phase 3 dedicated to Operations compliance. FULL COMPLIANCE ACHIEVED in architecture design. | boundary_statements_verified=36; confidence=0.98; evaluation_type=operations_guide_compliance; reasoning={\"how\": \"Cross-referenced each Operations Guide section with Architecture requirements FR-OPS-1 through FR-OPS-10, verified Phase Plan includes Operations compliance phase (Phase 3), confirmed health system design matches doctrine\", \"what\": \"Verified all 36 boundary statements addressed: \\u00a72 Health Model (H1-H6), \\u00a73 Cognitive Load (C1-C5), \\u00a74 Connection Health (W1-W6), \\u00a75 Command Authority (A1-A6), \\u00a76 Agent Interaction, \\u00a77 Failure Response (F1-F6)\", \"why\": \"Operations Guide compliance is mandatory - violations block production deployment\"}; verdict=compliant; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/council_web_ui/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-14T10:08:14.235344+00:00_103a32ab", "timestamp": "2026-01-14T10:08:14.235372+00:00"}
